(* Exercise 12, after lesson 12. A force F0 cos(w t). The antiderivative of cos(w u) is sin(w u)/w; one entry more than lesson 12.
   Solution: tutorial/solutions/12-ode.dx *)
goal v(t) == v(0) + F0*sin(w*t)/(m*w) @ m > 0, w > 0, t >= 0 functions v/1 assuming eom: m*D[s] v(s) == F0*cos(w*s) for s in [0, oo); regv: v in C^1 for s in [0, oo).

